{
  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485, F1 0.464), the dominant uncertainty is whether adding image information in a multimodal setup meaningfully improves over the RNA-only baseline. Config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the minimal, clean extension of config_001: it keeps the same RNA encoder (pca_n2000) and profile setting (singleprofile) while adding a ResNet50 image branch with concat fusion. This isolates the effect of multimodal fusion as the single changed factor, making the comparison to config_001 directly interpretable. If config_016 substantially outperforms config_001, it validates the multimodal direction and justifies subsequent experiments exploring better image encoders, multiprofile aggregation, and fusion strategies within the multimodal family. If it does not, it tells us the bottleneck lies elsewhere (e.g., RNA encoder quality or profile representation), redirecting the search toward RNA-side improvements. Under a tight budget, resolving this fundamental modality question first maximizes the information gained per experiment and prevents wasting runs on a suboptimal branch."
}

